  <text xml:lang="grc"><body xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.dindorf1893-grc1"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.dindorf1893-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades"><head>ΠΕΛΙΑΔΕΣ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1_2" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-1_2" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:601">
            <note type="source">1, 2. Eurip. Med. 688.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Τί χρῆμα δράσας; φράζε μοι σαφέστερον.</l>
            </lg>
            <note type="commentary">ad quem locum Schol. adnotat: σεσημείωται ὁ στίχος, ὅτι καὶ ἐν Πελιάσιν ἐστὶν, ὧν ἡ ἀρχή· Μήδεια, πρὸς μὲν δώμασιν τυραννικοῖς – Ita ex correctione Valck. Diatr. p. 200 legitur pro vulg. πολιάσιν ἄρχει μήδεια-δώμασι. Haud dubie Welck. recte prologum Medeæ tribuit et ad eundem refert versum, quem sine auctoris et fabulæ nomine citat Chœrobosc. ad Theodos. apud Bekk. An. Gr. p. 1309 b. (a Bekkero etiam p. 1447 Euripidi vindicatum):</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">Αἴσωνος υἱὸς Κρηθέως ἀφ᾽ αἵματος.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="3" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-3" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:606">
            <note type="source">3. Orion. Anthologn. (farrag. Eurip. nr. 5. post tit. VIII.) p. 55 ed. Schneidew. Stob. Ecl. Ethic. II, p. 336 ed. Heer.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Οὐκ ἔστι τὰ θεῶν ἄδικ᾽, ἐν ἀνθρώποισι δὲ</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">κακοῖς νοσοῦντα σύγχυσιν πολλὴν ἔχει.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="4" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-4" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:604">
            <note type="source">4. Stobæus Floril. III, 22. Schol. Pind. Pyth. II, 173.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Πρὸς κέντρα μὴ λάκτιζε τοῖς κρατοῦσί σου.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="5" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-5" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:605">
            <note type="source">5. Stobæus XLIX, 7.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Τὸ δ᾽ ἔσχατον δὴ τοῦτο θαυμαστὸν βροτοῖς,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">τυραννίς· οὐχ εὕροις ἂν ἀθλιώτερον.</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">φίλους τε πορθεῖν καὶ κατακτανεῖν χρεών·</l>
              <l n="4" xml:lang="grc">πλεῖστος φόβος πρόσεστι, μὴ δράσωσί τι.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="6" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-6" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades">
            <note type="source">6. Stobæus LXXIV, 26.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Αἰνῶ˙ διδάξαι δ᾽, ὦ τέκνον, σὲ βούλομαι</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="7" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-7" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:607">
            <note type="source">7. Stobæus XCII, 4.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ὁρῶσι δ᾽ οἱ διδόντες εἰς τὰ χρήματα.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="8" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-8" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:616">
            <note type="source">8. Æl. Hist. An. VII, 47. τῶν δὲ ὑστρέχων καὶ τῶν τοιούτων ἀγρίων τὰ ἔκγονα ὄβρια καλεῖται καὶ μέμνηται Εὐριπίδης ἐν Πελιάσι τοῦ ὀνόματος καὶ Αἰσχύλος ἐν Ἀγαμέμνονι καὶ Δικτυουλκοῖς.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="9" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-9" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:610">
            <note type="source">9. Joan. Damasc. in Gaisf. Append. ad Stobæum vol. IV. p. 12, Εὐριπίδου Πελιάσι·</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Φθείρου· τὸ γὰρ δρᾶν οὐκ ἔχων λόγους ἔχεις.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="10" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-10" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:609">
            <note type="source">10. Ibid. p. 20, et p. 33.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ὁ γὰρ ξυνὼν, κακὸς μὲν ἦν τύχῃ γεγὼς,</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">τοιούσδε τοὺς ξυνόντας ἐκπαιδεύεται,</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">χρηστοὺς δ᾽ ὁ χρηστός· ἀλλὰ τὰς ὁμιλίας</l>
              <l n="4" xml:lang="grc">ἐσθλὰς διώκειν, ὦ νέοι, σπουδάζετε.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="11" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-11" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:608">
            <note type="source">11. Ibid. p. 31.</note>
            <lg type="fragment">
              <l n="1" xml:lang="grc">Ἐν τοῖσι μὲν δεινοίσιν ὡς φίλοι φίλων</l>
              <l n="2" xml:lang="grc">ὅταν δὲ πράξωσ᾽ εὐ, διωθοῦνται χάριν,</l>
              <l n="3" xml:lang="grc">αὐτοὶ δι᾽ αὑτοὺς εὐτυχεῖν ἡγούμενοι.</l>
            </lg>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="12" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-12" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades">
            <note type="source">12. Hesych. Ἀρταμεῖν, κατακόπτειν. Εὐριπίδης Πολιάσιν. (sic). Idem Ἀντεμμάσσασθαι, ἀνταποδοῦναι, ἐπιπλῆξαι. Εὐριπίδης Πολιάσιν.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="13" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-13" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:613">
            <note type="source">13. Lexic. Sangermann. in Bekk. An. Gr. p. 95, 23. Εὐστόχως. Εὐριπίδης Πελιάσιν.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="14" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-14" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:615">
            <note type="source">14. Ibid. p. 106, 27. Λύσιμον θηλυκῶς λέγει Εὐριπίδης Πελιάσιν.</note>
          </div>
          <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="15" xml:id="fragment-peliades-dindorf1893_grc1-15" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0006_peliades" sameAs="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0006.peliades.nauck1889grc1:614">
            <note type="source">15. Schol. Plat. p. 137 Ruhnk. Κατηβολὴ, τὸ ἐπιβάλλον. Εὐριπίδης Τημένῳ καὶ Πελιάσι. Vide et Elms. ad Eur. Me. 1019, 20.</note>
          </div>
        </div></body></text></TEI>
